    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3589",
      "problem": "Is the function $y=g(x)$ below left-continuous at $x=0?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14262490/assets/03166feaa94b64b4fbdfac1096b0e0d771abf5b4a47e84a6e28dbed257540c6b.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To determine whether $g(x),$ is left-continuous at $x=0,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nIndeed, we see that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 0^-} g(x) = -2 = g(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=0.$",
